# SPA fallback, read by Netlify and Cloudflare Pages.
#
# The build writes a real HTML file for every route in src/seo.ts, and a file
# that exists always wins over a rule here — so /about is served its own
# stamped <head>, not this. The rule is only what catches a URL no route
# claims, so a deep link never 404s before React can route it.
#
# 200, not 301: a redirect would change the address bar and lose the path the
# router needs to read.
/*  /index.html  200
